1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
My name is Luna Deitch. I've been doing this for 30 years.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
For the first 16 years I couldn't get anybody to come out with me because nobody wanted to see this harrah.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
But I come from 18 generations of rabbis, orthodox rabbis.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Nobody, nobody in my family did this. Nobody. No rabbi.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
You can use a sack of money instead of swinging a chicken.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
And you know, I was talking to the kids and the kids are under the misconception that this is in the Torah.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It's not. Not in the Torah. It's not in the Talmud.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
It's in Shulchan Aruch, which was written in the 1500s by a Spanish rabbi by the name of Joseph K.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
And he called it a foolish custom.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:01,000
And unfortunately, shortly thereafter, an Ashkenazi rabbi from Eastern Europe came and he removed the negative commentary.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
And he thought it was a good idea to do and he promoted things as a chicken.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
That's why this is going on now.

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,000
And it's, it's not only violating 15 city and state laws, it's violating Jewish law.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The most important one is the Torah mandate not to cause harm to animals, unnecessary harm, and to help them if you can.

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
And there's also a Talmudic imperative in the Talmud that says feed your animals before you feed yourself.

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
These chickens don't get any food and water.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
And as you probably have seen, there are dead ones.

18
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
They die of dehydration and starvation and heat prostration.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:59,000
And when it's cold, because it goes by the Jewish calendar, sometimes it happens later in the year, it could be freezing.

20
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
They freeze to death, you know.

21
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:12,000
It was at this location once where it was raining and we captured, one of our activists captured video of them shivering and freezing to death.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
It's really an awful custom.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,000
It can be easily done with money and there's no excuse.

24
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
There's no excuse for this.

25
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
This is just blatant animal cruelty.

26
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
I've already seen two chickens with their wings broken, open fractures.

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
I'm a nurse by profession.

28
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
You could see the bones jutting on them and the guys holding them by the wings.

29
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:51,000
We tried to, sometimes community affairs will work with us and speak to the owner of the place and negotiate the release of the injured chickens.

30
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,000
But the guys covering right now, they're just doing overtime, they're not even from this precinct.

31
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:05,000
So they, you know, one of the officers went in to talk to the owner and was told that the owner's not there.

32
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
I don't believe that for a minute.

33
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
I'm sure the owner is there and it's just, it's just really awful.

34
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
It's horrible.

35
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Horrible.

36
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
But we're trying to change that.

37
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
We used to do angry protests.

38
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,000
They don't work.

39
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
You know, it just makes them dig their heels in more.

40
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
This is a very insolent community.

41
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You know, they, they are conditioned from birth to believe that this is a good thing to do.

42
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Sometimes when the kids cry and they tug at their mother's skirts and they say,

43
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
the chicken is crying, the chicken is crying.

44
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
The mothers tell them, oh, they're not crying.

45
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
They're happy to, they're singing.

46
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
They're happy to do this.

47
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,000
But if I'm there, I tell them, no, you're right.

48
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
I tell the kids, I said, they are crying because it hurts them.

49
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
I tell them, like, who provided?

50
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Thank you for documenting this.

51
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Yeah.

52
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,000
I appreciate it.

53
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:05,000
And all the prophets, Jeremiah, Yeremiyahu, Hosea, they say God wants mercy, not sacrifice.

54
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Exactly.

55
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Exactly.

56
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:15,000
This goes against every, you know, compassionate tenet in the Bible, in the Torah, in the Talmud.

57
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
It's just, it's an abomination.

58
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
And it's an embarrassment to me as a Jewish person.

59
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
You know, I think this is a stain on Judaism.

60
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:32,000
You know, I come from 18 generations of Orthodox rabbis, but I am not religious myself.

61
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:42,000
However, I'm very Jewish ethnically, you know, and I try to protect my, you know, my ethnicity.

62
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Sorry, it's okay.

63
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
I'm a nurse by profession.

64
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
I became a nurse in 1979.

65
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
I'm disabled now.

66
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
I can't work as a nurse anymore.

67
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:57,000
But, you know, I became a nurse because I can't stand to see anybody suffer without trying

68
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
to help or trying to prevent that suffering.

69
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
And it's the same reason I became a vegan 40 years ago.

70
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Same reason I'm here with the chickens.

71
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
So, you know.

72
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:18,000
As a Jew, but also a vegan, do you feel that what's happening here is really that much different

73
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
from what's happening in a Chick-fil-A slaughterhouse?

74
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
It isn't.

75
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
It is not much different.

76
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Except that the fact that they're really being tortured and they're being, you know, swung by their broken wings.

77
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:39,000
My cousin's a veterinarian in England and he said the wings are way too fragile to hold these big bodies.

78
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
These bodies are plumped up for their flesh.

79
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
And they're only babies.

80
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
They're five to six weeks old.

81
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Um, no, I don't, you know, it just hurts me on every level you can imagine.

82
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:59,000
What do you, what would you say to someone who finds this appalling as you do, but also eats chickens?

83
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Oh, that's happened many times.

84
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:09,000
When I was working in the hospital and I would show people what goes on, you know, during the ritual.

85
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,000
And they would be absolutely horrified while they're eating a chicken sandwich.

86
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:20,000
And I would say, you know what, the chicken you're eating suffered similarly, suffered just as much as these chickens.

87
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:34,000
And in a way, I mean, I, this is sort of important for people to see because maybe, just maybe, one makes them think about what they're eating.

88
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:40,000
You know, I know people have said to me when they've seen this, some people have said, I can't eat chicken anymore.

89
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Well, good, that's the first step, you know, but I mean, all animals, all animals suffer.

90
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
All sentient creatures.

91
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
And I try to talk to them.

92
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
I talk to them.

93
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
I talk to people all the time, all the time.

94
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:05,000
And, you know, I mean, I'm kind of glad that this is happening out in the street so people can see it.

95
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,000
You know, um, they need to see what they're responsible for.

96
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Chicken factories are behind walls.

97
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Right.

98
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Exactly.

99
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:22,000
And in my neighborhood of Borough Park, my orthodox neighborhood where I live, they've covered everything up since we've been out, you know, doing what we do.

100
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
And so nobody sees it here.

101
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,000
It's out in the open and everybody can see it.

102
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:49,000
So, I mean, I'm glad that it's in the, I'm glad that it's in the street so everybody who lives in the neighborhood and everybody driving through can see this because they need to make, start making connections to what they're eating.

103
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
They have to start making connections.

